From: gt-be98-buildroot <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: a failed MLD ADD no longer kills a -g hostapd and every
 interface it runs

Two crashes, both reproduced on mac80211_hwsim with hostapd 2.12 and with
upstream hostap 6d3d778 (2026-11-10), both on the global control interface's
ADD (hostapd_add_iface) while other interfaces run in the same process:

1. An AP MLD on a driver without MLO support (WPA_DRIVER_FLAGS2_MLO unset):
   hostapd_driver_init() returns -1 after hapd_init() but before any link is
   added. On a wiphy whose nl80211 driver context is shared with a running
   interface, hostapd_cleanup_driver() takes the MLD link-removal path,
   driver_nl80211_link_remove() removes the BSS and then delivers
   EVENT_MLD_INTERFACE_FREED to a NULL context: SEGV in
   wpa_supplicant_event() (drv_callbacks.c). Fix: clear conf->mld_ap on that
   failure, so the BSS is torn down as the plain BSS it still is.

2. A non-first link the driver refuses (start_ap -EBUSY): the setup failure
   already removed the link from the MLD (hostapd_mld_remove_link), then
   hostapd_add_iface()'s cleanup (hostapd_bss_link_deinit) removes it again;
   dl_list_del() on the cleared node dereferences NULL. Fix: make
   hostapd_mld_remove_link() a no-op for a BSS that is not on the list.

After the fix the ADD answers FAIL, the process and its other interfaces
keep running (an MLD's surviving first link included).
Test: package/gt-be98-os/test/hostapd-mld-hwsim-test.sh.

diff -ru a/hostapd/main.c b/hostapd/main.c
--- a/hostapd/main.c
+++ b/hostapd/main.c
@@ -371,6 +371,13 @@
 		if (!(iface->drv_flags2 & WPA_DRIVER_FLAGS2_MLO)) {
 			wpa_printf(MSG_INFO,
 				   "MLD: Not supported by the driver");
+			/* No link was added: let the caller tear this BSS down
+			 * as a plain BSS. As an MLD link, a driver context shared
+			 * with the other interfaces of the wiphy takes the
+			 * link-removal path, which then delivers
+			 * EVENT_MLD_INTERFACE_FREED to a NULL context and the
+			 * whole process dies. */
+			hapd->conf->mld_ap = 0;
 			return -1;
 		}
 
diff -ru a/src/ap/hostapd.c b/src/ap/hostapd.c
--- a/src/ap/hostapd.c
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.c
@@ -5317,6 +5317,13 @@
 	if (!mld)
 		return -1;
 
+	/* Not on the list: never added, or already removed (dl_list_del()
+	 * clears the pointers). A non-first link whose setup failed is
+	 * removed by that failure and again by the cleanup of
+	 * hostapd_add_iface(); the second dl_list_del() dereferenced NULL. */
+	if (!hapd->link.next || !hapd->link.prev)
+		return 0;
+
 	dl_list_del(&hapd->link);
 	mld->num_links--;
 
